# SP-Alpha-Rig control profile -- configuration.
# Sourced by ./rig. Every value is overridable from the environment.
#
# This file is the SINGLE source of truth for how the rig is addressed.
# Do not hardcode any of these values in a script, a brief, or a dispatch.

# --- The VM -------------------------------------------------------------
RIG_DOM="${RIG_DOM:-SP-Alpha-Rig}"

# libvirt USER-SESSION connection. The rig runs as chris, not as root.
# qemu:///system is a different, empty libvirt -- pointing there finds no domain.
RIG_URI="${RIG_URI:-qemu:///session}"

# --- The host that owns the VM -----------------------------------------
RIG_HOST_NAME="${RIG_HOST_NAME:-beelink}"
RIG_HOST_ADDR="${RIG_HOST_ADDR:-192.168.1.190}"
RIG_HOST_USER="${RIG_HOST_USER:-chris}"

# Key used to reach the Beelink from off-box (CT105 has this; on the Beelink
# itself it is unused because the libvirt calls are local).
RIG_HOST_KEY="${RIG_HOST_KEY:-$HOME/.ssh/beelink}"

# --- The guest ----------------------------------------------------------
RIG_USER="${RIG_USER:-sp}"

# Guest SSH key. Same keypair fleet-wide so ClaudeBox, Tom and Bee are
# interchangeable. Public half is installed into the guest by `rig bootstrap`.
RIG_KEY="${RIG_KEY:-$HOME/.ssh/spvm}"

# Guest address. Leave EMPTY -- `rig` discovers it from the guest agent on
# every call and caches it for the process. Set it only to pin a known IP.
RIG_IP="${RIG_IP:-}"

# LUKS passphrase for the dev image. Dev-only credential for a throwaway
# test VM; it is not a production secret and never leaves this repo.
RIG_LUKS="${RIG_LUKS:-spplustest}"

# --- Artefacts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots land here on the HOST, as a path RELATIVE TO THE HOST USER'S
# HOME (an ssh session starts there). `rig shot` copies them back to the
# caller when the caller is off-box. Keep it relative -- an absolute path
# would need expanding on the far side and silently lands in the wrong home.
RIG_SHOTDIR="${RIG_SHOTDIR:-logs/sp-plus/SP-Alpha-Rig/shots}"
